    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n81730" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περινέω</span></b>  (B), <i><span class="en">
			Hdt.
			6.80
		</span></i> : aor.
		part.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περινήσας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					4.164
				</span></i>
			, also un
				contr.
			
			inf. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νηῆσαι</span>
			v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				2.107
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Q.S.
				3.678
			</span></i> (
				Med.
			):—<i>pile, heap round</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕλην</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ
				τὸν πύργον</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.164
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολὺ πῦρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Anon.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.583a
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τὴν οἰκίην ὕλῃ</span>
			<i>pile it round</i> with wood, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.107
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕλῃ τὸ ἄλσος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					6.80
				</span></i>
			.</div>
